# Lab 20 Experiment 3: Create a Registration with a companion source ID
#
# Question:
# Can one separately managed Agent Registration be created with:
# - a deterministic companion source ID distinct from the provider source ID;
# - a newly created disposable platform Blueprint;
# - its enabled Blueprint principal; and
# - a newly created Agent Identity;
# while the original Registry Sync Package remains unchanged?
#
# The earlier GCP experiment returned 201 and successful readback. This file
# reconstructs that controlled request for a different explicitly approved
# disposable source. Do not resend it for the source that already has a
# companion or an unresolved create.
#
# All real values come from the shared ignored ../../.env:
#
# A365_EXP3_TARGET_NAME=<selected-package-display-name>
# A365_EXP3_PACKAGE_ID=<registry-sync-package-id>
# A365_EXP3_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-provider-source-agent-id>
# A365_EXP3_SOURCE_CREATED_AT=<exact-source-created-timestamp>
# A365_EXP3_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT=<exact-source-modified-timestamp>
# A365_EXP3_BLUEPRINT_GROUP=<approved-disposable-platform-group-label>
# A365_EXP3_CREATED_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH=<leave-empty-until-Step-3.12>
# A365_EXP3_CREATED_PACKAGE_ID=<leave-empty-until-Step-3.13>
#
# Evidence belongs only under:
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@targetName = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_TARGET_NAME}}
@packageId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_PACKAGE_ID}}
@providerSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@sourceCreatedAt = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_SOURCE_CREATED_AT}}
@sourceModifiedAt = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT}}
@blueprintGroup = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_BLUEPRINT_GROUP}}
@createdRegistrationIdPath = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_CREATED_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH}}
@createdPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3_CREATED_PACKAGE_ID}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@experimentScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Create%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Create%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Create.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Step 3.1 - Authenticate
#
# DO NOT SAVE either authentication response or the /me response.

# @name exp3DeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{experimentScopes}}

###

# Complete browser sign-in before sending this request.

# @name exp3Token
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{exp3DeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

# @name exp3CurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.2 - List inventory and select one GCP Package
#
# Expected: 200. Save the first response as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/package-list-page-1.json
#
# If @odata.nextLink is present, send a GET to that exact URL and save later
# responses as package-list-page-2.json, package-list-page-3.json, and so on
# until the latest response has no @odata.nextLink.
#
# Across all saved pages, select exactly one approved, disposable Package with:
# - platform equal to GoogleVertexAI;
# - Connected Platform source metadata; and
# - no existing or unresolved companion mapping.
#
# Copy its values into the shared ignored ../../.env:
#
# A365_EXP3_TARGET_NAME=<exact-selected-package-displayName>
# A365_EXP3_PACKAGE_ID=<exact-selected-package-id>
#
# Save .env and reload REST Client before Step 3.3. Do not select by name alone
# when duplicate display names exist.

# @name exp3ListPackages
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.3 - Read the selected Package Details
#
# Expected: 200. Before copying any value, save the complete response as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/package-before-create.json
#
# Open the saved JSON and confirm id, displayName, and platform match the
# selection from Step 3.2. From its nested Connected Platform definition, copy
# the exact values into:
#
# A365_EXP3_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-SourceAgentId>
# A365_EXP3_SOURCE_CREATED_AT=<exact-CreatedDateTime>
# A365_EXP3_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT=<exact-LastModifiedDateTime>
#
# Preserve SourceAgentId byte-for-byte. Save .env and reload REST Client before
# any create request.

# @name exp3PackageBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{packageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3A - approve one disposable platform Blueprint
#
# The selected Registry Sync Package has no Blueprint or Agent Identity. That
# absence does not prove that no reusable platform Blueprint exists, so first
# reconcile protected platform/group mapping. Continue only when:
# - A365_EXP3_BLUEPRINT_GROUP is the approved disposable platform boundary;
# - no approved reusable Blueprint is recorded for this platform/group;
# - no earlier Blueprint create has an unresolved outcome; and
# - creating one disposable Blueprint is explicitly authorized.

###############################################################################
# Step 3.4 - Create the disposable platform Blueprint
#
# DO NOT SEND until Stop 3A is satisfied.
# Expected: 201. Save the response or safe error body as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/blueprint-create-response.json
#
# On timeout, 5xx, or another ambiguous result, stop and do not retry.

# @name exp3CreateBlueprint
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "displayName": "GoogleVertexAI - {{blueprintGroup}} - disposable Blueprint",
  "sponsors@odata.bind": [
    "{{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/users/{{exp3CurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ],
  "owners@odata.bind": [
    "{{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/users/{{exp3CurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ]
}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.5 - Verify the created Blueprint
#
# Run only after Step 3.4 returned 201. Expected: 200.
# Save the response as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/blueprint-after-create.json

# @name exp3GetCreatedBlueprint
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{exp3CreateBlueprint.response.body.$.id}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.6 - Check whether the Blueprint principal already exists
#
# Expected: 200 or a definite 404. Save the response or safe error body as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/blueprint-principal-before-create.json
#
# A 403 or another error is a stop condition, not permission to create.

# @name exp3GetBlueprintPrincipal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{exp3GetCreatedBlueprint.response.body.$.appId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3B - approve one Blueprint principal creation
#
# Send Step 3.7 only when Step 3.6 returned a definite 404, no earlier
# principal create is unresolved, and one creation is explicitly authorized.
# Skip Step 3.7 when Step 3.6 returned 200.

###############################################################################
# Step 3.7 - Create the missing Blueprint principal
#
# Expected: 201. Save the response or safe error body as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/blueprint-principal-create-response.json
#
# On timeout, 5xx, or another ambiguous result, stop and do not retry.

# @name exp3CreateBlueprintPrincipal
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "appId": "{{exp3GetCreatedBlueprint.response.body.$.appId}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.8 - Verify the Blueprint principal
#
# Run after Step 3.6 returned 200 or Step 3.7 returned 201. Expected: 200.
# Confirm appId matches the Blueprint and accountEnabled is not false.
# Save the response as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/blueprint-principal-after-create.json

# @name exp3VerifyBlueprintPrincipal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{exp3GetCreatedBlueprint.response.body.$.appId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3C - approve one Agent Identity creation
#
# Continue only when:
# - the Blueprint and enabled principal were verified;
# - the selected GCP source belongs to the approved Blueprint group;
# - no Agent Identity or unresolved identity create exists for this source; and
# - one Agent Identity creation is explicitly authorized.

###############################################################################
# Step 3.9 - Create the Agent Identity under the Blueprint
#
# Expected: 201. Save the response or safe error body as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/agent-identity-create-response.json
#
# On timeout, 5xx, or another ambiguous result, stop and do not retry.

# @name exp3CreateAgentIdentity
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "displayName": "{{targetName}} - managed Agent Identity",
  "agentIdentityBlueprintId": "{{exp3GetCreatedBlueprint.response.body.$.appId}}",
  "sponsors@odata.bind": [
    "{{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/users/{{exp3CurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ]
}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.10 - Verify the created Agent Identity
#
# Run only after Step 3.9 returned 201. Expected: 200.
# Confirm agentIdentityBlueprintId matches the Blueprint appId and
# servicePrincipalType is ServiceIdentity. Save the response as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/agent-identity-after-create.json

# @name exp3GetCreatedAgentIdentity
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{exp3CreateAgentIdentity.response.body.$.id}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3D - approve exactly one companion Registration create
#
# Continue only when:
# - the Package and exact provider source match the selected inventory record;
# - the new Agent Identity belongs to the new Blueprint;
# - no active or unresolved companion mapping exists for this provider source;
# - the target is disposable and approved; and
# - one Registration create attempt is explicitly authorized.
#
# The Registration source is deliberately different from the provider source:
#
# agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:<exact-provider-source-agent-id>

###############################################################################
# Step 3.11 - Create the companion Registration
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: response body and safe error body as:
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/registration-create-response.json
# Record the HTTP status in the same JSON result. On timeout or 5xx, stop and
# do not retry.

# @name exp3CreateCompanion
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

{
  "displayName": "{{targetName}} - managed companion",
  "description": "Disposable independently managed companion registration",
  "createdBy": "{{exp3CurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}",
  "ownerIds": [
    "{{exp3CurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ],
  "sourceAgentId": "agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:{{providerSourceAgentId}}",
  "originatingStore": "GoogleVertexAI",
  "sourceCreatedDateTime": "{{sourceCreatedAt}}",
  "sourceLastModifiedDateTime": "{{sourceModifiedAt}}",
  "agentIdentityBlueprintId": "{{exp3GetCreatedBlueprint.response.body.$.appId}}",
  "agentIdentityId": "{{exp3GetCreatedAgentIdentity.response.body.$.id}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.12 - Convert the returned Registration ID and read it back
#
# The Registration create response can return an id containing `%2F`. This id
# is distinct from A365_EXP3_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID. Keep the provider source
# value unchanged because it is used in the JSON create body.
#
# Before sending this GET:
#
# 1. Copy and run this one-line command in PowerShell:
#
# [uri]::EscapeDataString((Read-Host 'Paste Registration id').Trim()) | Set-Clipboard
#
# 2. When prompted, copy the exact `id` from the saved
#    registration-create-response.json, paste it into PowerShell, and press
#    Enter.
# 3. Paste the converted clipboard value into the ignored .env:
#
# A365_EXP3_CREATED_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH=<path-safe-created-registration-id>
#
# 4. Save .env and reload REST Client. An original `%2F` must appear as
#    `%252F` in this path-only variable.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED:
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/registration-after-create.json

# @name exp3GetCreatedCompanion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{createdRegistrationIdPath}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.13 - List Packages after Registration creation
#
# Registration creation can also materialize a new Package, but this experiment
# must not assume its Package ID equals the Registration ID.
#
# Save the first response as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/package-list-after-create-page-1.json
#
# If @odata.nextLink is present, save later pages as
# package-list-after-create-page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on until the latest
# response has no @odata.nextLink.
#
# Across all pages, identify both records independently:
#
# 1. Original Registry Sync Package:
#    - id equals A365_EXP3_PACKAGE_ID;
#    - platform is GoogleVertexAI; and
#    - nested source equals A365_EXP3_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID.
#
# 2. Newly materialized companion Package:
#    - source matches the companion source from Step 3.11;
#    - Blueprint and Agent Identity links match the created objects; and
#    - it is not selected only by display name.
#
# Copy the new Package's top-level id into the ignored .env:
#
# A365_EXP3_CREATED_PACKAGE_ID=<new-companion-package-id>
#
# If the second Package is not present yet, record that observation, wait for
# the agreed propagation period, and repeat this read-only list. Do not create
# another Registration.
#
# @name exp3ListPackagesAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.14 - Confirm the original Registry Sync Package is unchanged
#
# SAVE REQUIRED:
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/original-package-after-create.json

# @name exp3OriginalPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{packageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3.15 - Read the newly materialized companion Package
#
# Run only after Step 3.13 found one unambiguous new Package ID.
# Confirm its companion source, Blueprint, Agent Identity, owner, and platform.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED:
# ../../evidence/experiments/03-companion-source-registration-create/companion-package-after-create.json

# @name exp3CompanionPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{createdPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3Token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Finalize - save the complete mapping
#
# Save the provider source, current Package ID, companion source, returned
# Registration ID, Blueprint object ID and app ID, Blueprint principal ID, and
# Agent Identity ID in protected local state. Record that all three Entra
# objects were created by this experiment. Do not delete them until the rename
# and delete demos have completed or separate cleanup is approved.
